    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>6. Offline Mission Package Specification</h2>
<p>
To ensure total autonomous recovery at sea, the backend pre-generates a bundled, signed JSON and vector package when a mission is initialized.
</p>
<pre>{
  "mission_id": "8f9a2b1c-7d4e-4f1a-b2c3-d4e5f6a7b8c9",
  "report_id": "3c4d5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f-3a4b5c6d7e8f",
  "prediction_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
  "offline_map_bbox": [80.10, 12.90, 80.45, 13.25],
  "offline_map_zoom_levels": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13],
  "drift_heatmap_geojson": {
    "type": "FeatureCollection",
    "features": [
      {
        "type": "Feature",
        "geometry": { "type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [...] },
        "properties": { "risk_level": "critical", "score": 88.5, "forecast_hour": 48 }
      }
    ]
  },
  "recommended_route_geojson": {
    "type": "Feature",
    "geometry": { "type": "LineString", "coordinates": [...] },
    "properties": { "total_distance_nm": 14.2, "estimated_patrol_hours": 3.5 }
  },
  "high_risk_zones_geojson": { ... },
  "reported_loss_point": { "latitude": 13.1122, "longitude": 80.2937 },
  "weather_snapshot": {
    "current_velocity_knots": 1.2,
    "current_direction_deg": 45.0,
    "wave_height_m": 1.4,
    "wind_speed_knots": 12.0
  },
  "generated_at": "2026-10-04T07:15:00Z"
}</pre>

<h2>7. Comprehensive Database Schema</h2>

<h3>7.1 Server-Side PostgreSQL + PostGIS Schema</h3>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Table Name</th>
            <th>Primary Columns & Types</th>
            <th>Indexes & Constraints</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>users</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), name (VARCHAR), phone (VARCHAR), role (ENUM), boat_id (UUID), created_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)</td>
            <td>PK(id), UNIQUE(phone)</td>
            <td>Stores fishers, recovery team personnel, recyclers, and system administrators.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>boats</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), name (VARCHAR), registration_number (VARCHAR), harbour (VARCHAR), owner_id (UUID)</td>
            <td>PK(id), UNIQUE(registration_number), FK(owner_id)</td>
            <td>Vessels registered at Kasimedu and adjacent coastal landing sites.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>gear</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), gear_type (VARCHAR), material (VARCHAR), weight_kg (FLOAT), qr_code (VARCHAR), owner_id (UUID)</td>
            <td>PK(id), UNIQUE(qr_code), FK(owner_id)</td>
            <td>Pre-registered fishing gear inventories with material signatures.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>lost_gear_reports</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), client_report_id (UUID), gear_id (UUID), reported_by (UUID), loss_location (GEOMETRY(Point, 4326)), loss_time (TIMESTAMPTZ), photo_url (TEXT), sync_status (VARCHAR)</td>
            <td>PK(id), UNIQUE(client_report_id), GIST(loss_location), FK(reported_by)</td>
            <td>Lost gear incidents reported by fishers with spatial coordinates.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>drift_predictions</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), report_id (UUID), forecast_hours (INT), heatmap_geojson (JSONB), predicted_path_geojson (JSONB), high_risk_zones_geojson (JSONB), confidence_score (FLOAT)</td>
            <td>PK(id), FK(report_id), GIN(heatmap_geojson)</td>
            <td>Simulation results containing probabilistic drift envelopes.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>recovery_missions</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), prediction_id (UUID), team_id (UUID), boat_id (UUID), status (ENUM), search_area (GEOMETRY(Polygon, 4326)), planned_route (GEOMETRY(LineString, 4326))</td>
            <td>PK(id), GIST(search_area), FK(team_id)</td>
            <td>Active and completed recovery operations at sea.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>recovery_updates</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), client_update_id (UUID), mission_id (UUID), report_id (UUID), status (ENUM), location (GEOMETRY(Point, 4326)), weight_kg (FLOAT), photo_url (TEXT)</td>
            <td>PK(id), UNIQUE(client_update_id), GIST(location)</td>
            <td>At-sea observations (net_spotted, net_recovered, not_found).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>recycler_assignments</code></td>
            <td>id (UUID), recovery_update_id (UUID), recycler_id (UUID), material_type (VARCHAR), weight_kg (FLOAT), status (ENUM)</td>
            <td>PK(id), FK(recovery_update_id), FK(recycler_id)</td>
            <td>Circular economy routing records connecting recovered gear to recyclers.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>7.2 Mobile Client SQLite Schema</h3>
<pre>-- Local Action Sync Queue
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS local_sync_queue (
    queue_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    action TEXT NOT NULL,                -- 'create_lost_gear_report' | 'create_recovery_update'
    client_entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,      -- UUIDv4 generated on device
    payload TEXT NOT NULL,               -- JSON serialized request body
    retry_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending',       -- 'pending' | 'syncing' | 'synced' | 'failed'
    last_error TEXT,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    synced_at TEXT
);

-- Local Mirror of Loss Reports
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS local_reports (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    client_report_id TEXT UNIQUE,
    gear_type TEXT,
    material TEXT,
    quantity INTEGER,
    latitude REAL,
    longitude REAL,
    loss_time TEXT,
    photo_uri TEXT,
    sync_status TEXT,
    created_at TEXT
);

-- Local Mission Packages
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS local_missions (
    mission_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    report_id TEXT,
    prediction_id TEXT,
    bounding_box TEXT,
    heatmap_geojson TEXT,
    route_geojson TEXT,
    high_risk_zones_geojson TEXT,
    status TEXT,
    downloaded_at TEXT
);</pre>

<h2>8. Circular Economy Impact Calculation Model</h2>
<p>
GhostNet AI quantifies verified ecological and carbon-reduction dividends for stakeholders and sustainability credits:
</p>

<h3>8.1 Greenhouse Gas Abatement ($\text{CO}_2\text{e}$ Avoided)</h3>
<pre>CO2e_Avoided (kg) = Recovered_Net_Weight (kg) * Material_Emission_Factor (kg CO2e/kg)</pre>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Nylon 6 (PA6) / Nylon 6,6</strong>: $\text{EF} = 6.5\text{ kg CO}_2\text{e per kg}$ (virgin polymer displacement factor)</li>
    <li><strong>High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE)</strong>: $\text{EF} = 2.1\text{ kg CO}_2\text{e per kg}$</li>
    <li><strong>Polypropylene (PP) Ropes</strong>: $\text{EF} = 1.9\text{ kg CO}_2\text{e per kg}$</li>
</ul>

<h3>8.2 Marine Fauna Entanglement Protection Metric</h3>
<p>
Based on empirical studies of ALDFG entrapment rates along the Coromandel coast:
</p>
<pre>Protected_Marine_Animals = Recovered_Net_Weight (kg) * 0.12</pre>
<p>
Where 100 kg of recovered gillnet corresponds to an estimated 12 marine animals (fish, turtles, juvenile sharks) protected from mortality over a 12-month drift horizon.
</p>

<h2>9. Security, RBAC & Deployment Topology</h2>

<h3>9.1 Authentication & Security Architecture</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>JWT Bearer Tokenization</strong>: Short-lived access tokens (1 hour) with long-lived refresh tokens (30 days) stored in Expo SecureStore.</li>
    <li><strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</strong>:
        <ul>
            <li><code>fisher</code>: Create and review personal lost gear reports.</li>
            <li><code>recovery_team</code>: View regional heatmaps, accept missions, download offline packages, write recovery updates.</li>
            <li><code>recycler</code>: View assigned materials, update batch processing statuses.</li>
            <li><code>admin</code>: Global command dashboard, risk model tuning, partner management, system telemetry.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Presigned S3 Uploads</strong>: Mobile clients upload photos directly to object storage via presigned URLs, keeping file payloads off the application API servers.</li>
</ul>

<h3>9.2 Docker Compose Deployment Architecture</h3>
<div class="diagram-box">
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                              DOCKER COMPOSE TOPOLOGY                                  |
|                                                                                       |
|   [Port 80/443]  --> [nginx-reverse-proxy]                                            |
|                           |                                                           |
|                           +---> [admin-web-dashboard] (Port 3000, Vite React SPA)     |
|                           +---> [fastapi-api-service] (Port 8000, Python 3.11 ASGI)   |
|                                     |                                                 |
|                                     +---> [postgres-postgis] (Port 5432)             |
|                                     +---> [redis-broker]     (Port 6379)             |
|                                     +---> [minio-storage]    (Port 9000/9001)        |
|                                                                                       |
|   [redis-broker] <-----------> [celery-drift-worker] (Particle Simulation / GIS)      |
|   [redis-broker] <-----------> [celery-beat-scheduler] (Periodic Met Sync & Sweeper)  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
</div>

